# Golden test fixtures are compared byte-for-byte (raw string equality, no
# line-ending normalization). On Windows, core.autocrlf=true converts these to
# CRLF on checkout, which breaks every TestGolden* test on a fresh clone.
# Pin them to LF so they are byte-identical across all platforms and checkouts.
testdata/golden/** text eol=lf

# Repository canon is LF for Go sources. With core.autocrlf=true on Windows the
# checkout is CRLF, so `gofmt -l` flags every file and the pre-commit gofmt leg
# fails. Pin Go sources to LF to keep worktrees and the index byte-identical.
*.go text eol=lf
